"GEORGIA INVESTMENT SPENDING SHOCK ANALYSIS"
"Demand-Side Macro Accounting Framework"

OVERVIEW
"This workbook estimates the impact of an $6.5 billion USD investment shock over 8 years (2026-2033) on Georgia's economy using a demand-side macro accounting framework."

"DATA SOURCES"
"1. IMF World Economic Outlook (WEO) Database"
"   - Nominal GDP, Real GDP, Growth Rates, Population"
"   - Data for 2021-2027 (historical and projections)"
"   - Extension to 2043 using constant growth assumptions"

"2. Geostat (National Statistics Office of Georgia)"
"   - Supply and Use Tables (Table 38-38)"
"   - Download from: https://www.geostat.ge/en/modules/categories/632/supply-and-use-tables-new"
"   - Use latest available (2024 recommended)"

"SHEETS DESCRIPTION"
"Sheet 1: WEO_Data"
"   - Macroeconomic baseline data from IMF"
"   - Contains: Nominal GDP, Real GDP, Growth Rates, GDP Deflator, Population"
"   - Extends from 2021 to 2043"
"   - Uses formula-based extension with average deflator growth (1.548%) and 5% real growth"

"Sheet 2: SUT_Calc"
"   - Supply and Use Table calculations"
"   - To be populated: Copy SUPPLY and USE sheets from Geostat Excel files"
"   - Column C-H: Link relevant data from geostat tables"
"   - Cell C46: Calculates import content share"

"Sheet 3: NA (National Accounts - Scenario 1: Baseline)"
"   - Main projection table with baseline assumptions"
"   - Assumptions: Multiplier = 0.8, Exchange Rate = 2.746 Lari/USD"
"   - Output: Annual demand, domestic/import breakdown, Real GDP impact"

"Sheet 4: NA_Scenario2 (Scenario 2: Higher Multiplier)"
"   - Same structure as Scenario 1 but with multiplier = 1.0"
"   - Shows sensitivity to demand multiplier assumption"

"Sheet 3: NA_Scenario3 (Scenario 3: Higher Import Content)"
"   - Same structure as Scenario 1 but with import content share = 0.5"
"   - Shows sensitivity to import content assumption"

"KEY FORMULAS AND ASSUMPTIONS"
"Investment Shock Calculation (8 years: 2026-2033):"
"   Annual Investment (USD mm) = Total Investment / Investment Period"
"   = 6,500 / 8 = 812.5 USD millions per year"

"Exchange Rate: 2.746 Lari/USD (fixed)"

"Investment Deflator: Uses GDP deflator from WEO_Data (row 7)"

"Demand Components:"
"   Domestic Demand = Nominal Investment × (1 - Import Share) × Multiplier"
"   Import Demand = Nominal Investment × Import Share × Multiplier"
"   Total Demand = Domestic + Import Demand"

"Real GDP Impact:"
"   = Domestic Demand / (Deflator/100) in billions USD"

"Growth Adjustment:"
"   = Real GDP Impact / Real GDP (from WEO) × 100 (%)"

"INSTRUCTIONS FOR USE"
"Step 1: Populate Supply and Use Table data"
"   - Visit geostat.ge and download latest Supply and Use Tables"
"   - Copy SUPPLY sheet and USE sheet into this workbook"
"   - In SUT_Calc sheet, link relevant data (Imports, Total Supply, Total Use, etc.)"
"   - Cell C46 will auto-calculate import content share"

"Step 2: Review all three scenarios"
"   - Compare results across Baseline, Higher Multiplier, and Higher Import Content scenarios"
"   - Each row shows annual impact over 2026-2033 period"

NOTES
"- All formulas are preserved in the workbook (no hardcoded values)"
"- GDP Deflator extended using 4-year average growth rate (1.548%)"
"- Real growth rate held constant at 5.0% from 2028-2043"
"- Investment is assumed to have bell-shaped distribution (equal annual amounts)"
"- Multiplier effect captures both direct and indirect demand"
"- Import content share determines domestic vs. external demand"
